{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Live rich-text cutover + state echo suppression + LWW conflict safety\n\n## Context / Problem\nThis story **cuts the live Cloud and DC send paths over to the now-capable rich\ncodecs** (delivered by `e59d` and `271c`, on which this story depends) and makes\nthat cutover echo-safe. Because the DC codec is one-way and lossy, loop prevention\ncannot rely on `decode(encode(x))==x`. Both clients must suppress echo by\n**state**: compare the current Jira value against the last-synced baseline the\nreconciler already keeps (ADR 0026, `binding_store.py:102`; `_BASELINE_FIELDS` at\n`:108`; `set_baseline` at `:459`). We must also not silently destroy either side's\nedits under concurrency, and any state we add must respect epic `0303`'s churn\ndiscipline (a per-pass timestamp there caused the tickets-store bloat this feature\nmust not regress).\n\n**Why the cutover lives HERE, not in the leaves.** `e59d`/`271c` deliver capable\ncodecs but deliberately leave the live send sites on the plain/identity path, so\nthat the observable format change and its echo-safety land **together** in one\nstory (this one), never a hazard-before-safety window.\n\n## Prior art in this repo (build on the existing convergence, do NOT re-invent it)\n- The rich-text COMPARE normalization already exists as the codec's\n  **`normalize_outbound`** op (`RichTextCodec`, `adapters/jira_family/rich_text.py`).\n  The description diff already routes every side through it / the equivalent\n  `adf.normalize_description`: `OutboundFieldMapper.map_fields_to_remote`\n  (`outbound_mapper.py:77`), `outbound_fields.py:564`, and `inbound_differ.py:210`\n  (Jira side at `:212`). This story adds the three-way BASELINE layer ON TOP of\n  that convergence; it does NOT add a second, parallel `norm()`.\n- `binding_store.py` already persists the last-synced baseline (ADR 0026); this\n  story extends that record, it does not create a new store.\n- The codec law `normalize_outbound(t) == decode_inbound(to_wire(t))`\n  (`test_rich_text_codec.py:163`) and the comment dedup that depends on it\n  (`outbound_comments.py:48`) are preserved by routing every compare through the\n  codec op.\n\n## The live cutover (both clients — this story's new scope)\nReroute the direct plain-encode call sites through the capable codecs so the wire\nactually carries rich text, and prove convergence:\n- **Cloud:** replace the direct `_text_to_adf` (= `adf.text_to_adf`) encode at\n  `adapters/jira/acli.py:205` and `acli_cli_ops.py:369` with the `AdfCodec`\n  wire op, and the direct `adf.normalize_description`/`adf.fit_text_to_adf_limit`\n  compare sites at `outbound_fields.py:564` and `inbound_differ.py:210` with the\n  codec's `normalize_outbound`/`fit_outbound`. Each already-synced description\n  re-emits **exactly once** (the `outbound_fields.py:564` once-only re-emit\n  mechanism) to upgrade to rich ADF, then converges.\n- **DC:** wire the pure `wiki_render.render_markdown_to_wiki` (from `271c`) into\n  `WikiTextCodec.to_wire`, and **redefine `WikiTextCodec.normalize_outbound` to the\n  compare form `decode_inbound(to_wire(t))`** so the codec law\n  (`test_rich_text_codec.py:163`) is re-established for the rendering codec. Because\n  DC's live send composes `normalize_outbound(fit_outbound(value))` at\n  `outbound_mapper.py:77`, this redefinition is exactly what makes\n  `issue.update(fields=…)` begin shipping rendered wiki — the cutover — so it\n  **must** land here with echo-safety, not in the leaf. Also apply `to_wire` on the\n  CREATE path at `backend.py:70`. Update the DC identity pin tests\n  (`test_wiki_normalize_is_identity`,\n  `test_wiki_codec_wire_shape_and_decode_are_the_plain_string`,\n  `test_non_string_values_pass_through_untouched`) to the rendering behavior.\n- **Rollback:** the cutover is gated behind a single switch (config/flag) that\n  restores the plain/identity path for that client without reverting the codec\n  capability, so a bad rollout is one revert, not a code rewrite.\n\n## Approach (echo-safety + concurrency)\nDrive body sync from a three-way state — `baseline` (last-synced Jira canonical\nform), `local` (rebar body), `remote` (current Jira value) — each normalized\nthrough the **existing codec `normalize_outbound`** (compare-only) before diffing.\nOutbound fires only when `local` differs from `baseline` (rebar-originated\nchange); a value equal to `baseline` is our own echo and is skipped. **The\nbaseline is the value OBSERVED AFTER push** — after pushing a changed field, GET\nit back and store Jira's canonicalized form as the new baseline (one extra GET,\nonly on change) — so a benign Jira re-canonicalization is never mistaken for a\nhuman edit. When both `local` and `remote` diverged from `baseline` (concurrent\nedit), apply last-write-wins to pick the winner but always emit a detectable\nconflict signal so nothing is silently lost. For the rich layer, store a\nchange-gated `rich_sha = sha256(rendered_wire)[:16]` (8 bytes) **inline** in the\nbinding (proven 0.07 KB/version stable, identical to the baseline profile; a\nper-pass timestamp was proven to reproduce 0303's 12.62 KB anti-pattern) so a\nre-render is only pushed when the wire actually changed. The compare stays\ncomparison-only and never writes back.\n\n## Scope\n- `adapters/jira/acli.py` (`:205`), `adapters/jira/acli_cli_ops.py` (`:369`),\n  `adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py` (`:564`), `inbound_differ.py` (`:210`) —\n  Cloud live cutover through `AdfCodec` (gated).\n- `adapters/jira_family/rich_text.py` — DC cutover: `WikiTextCodec.to_wire`\n  delegates to `wiki_render.render_markdown_to_wiki`; `normalize_outbound` set to\n  `decode_inbound(to_wire(t))` (re-establishes the codec law for the rendering\n  codec) — this is what makes `outbound_mapper.py:77` ship rendered wiki.\n- `adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py` (`:70`) — DC CREATE-path render (gated).\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_rich_text_codec.py` — update the DC identity\n  pin tests + codec-law test for the now-rendering `WikiTextCodec`.\n- `binding_store.py` — inline change-gated `rich_sha` beside the existing baseline\n  (`_BASELINE_FIELDS`); observed-after-push baseline update.\n- the existing description differ / compare path — three-way baseline diff + LWW\n  arbitration, reusing the codec `normalize_outbound` (NOT a new `norm()`, NOT\n  changing the shared plain-text `inbound_fields.normalize_rich_text`).\n- `tests/` — cutover, convergence, echo, conflict, and no-churn tests.\n\n## Testing\n- **Cloud convergence:** after the cutover, a converted ADF description posts once,\n  and a second reconcile pass emits **zero** description updates (`test_cloud_cutover_converges`).\n- **DC convergence:** a rendered-wiki description posts once and a second pass\n  emits zero description updates (`test_dc_cutover_converges`).\n- Self-echo: a rebar-originated body change propagates exactly once and a second\n  pass pushes nothing (0 echo-back).\n- Concurrent: both sides edit the same body; the pass records a conflict and\n  applies LWW without discarding the loser silently (799/799-detected invariant).\n- No-churn: a pass with no body change updates 0 `rich_sha` entries and writes no\n  timestamp; asserted by the git-delta cost harness (≤0.07 KB/version stable).\n- Rollback: with the cutover flag off, the wire reverts to the plain/identity\n  encode for that client (`test_cutover_rollback_restores_plain`).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] After the Cloud cutover, a converted ADF description posts once and a second\n  reconcile pass emits zero description updates; verified by\n  `test_cloud_cutover_converges`.\n- [ ] After the DC cutover, `issue.update(fields=…)` receives rendered wiki (not\n  raw Markdown) and a second pass emits zero description updates; verified by\n  `test_dc_cutover_converges`.\n- [ ] The three-way diff reuses the codec `normalize_outbound` for the compare and\n  adds no parallel normalizer; verified by `test_echo_uses_codec_normalize`.\n- [ ] Outbound fires only on a rebar-originated change and the baseline stored is\n  the value observed after push; verified by `test_echo_observed_after_push` (a\n  benign Jira re-canonicalization does not re-sync).\n- [ ] A concurrent both-sides edit is detected and flagged under LWW with the\n  losing side never silently destroyed; verified by\n  `test_concurrent_conflict_detected` (799/799 over the corpus sample).\n- [ ] The rich layer stores a change-gated inline 8-byte `rich_sha` and no\n  per-pass timestamp, changing 0 entries on a no-op pass; verified by the\n  git-delta cost harness reproducing the ≤0.07 KB/version stable profile.\n- [ ] The cutover is flag-gated and reverts to the plain/identity wire when off;\n  verified by `test_cutover_rollback_restores_plain`."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785809679835480001,"uuid":"d7846e17-a9d5-4137-b0d9-ad4104a6c151"}